//
// Runs the same check create and update run before accepting a targeting rule, and reports what it found without writing anything. A rule that references a fact or an entitlement that does not exist does not fail loudly at evaluation — it simply never matches — so this is what lets an editor say so while the rule is being written. A rejected rule is a 200 carrying `valid: false`, not a client error.
